   "install": {
    "title": "Self-hosting",
    "html": "<p><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/firecrawl/firecrawl/main/img/open-source-cloud.png\" alt=\"Open Source vs Cloud\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" /></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/firecrawl/firecrawl#firecrawl-local\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Firecrawl Local</a> is the easiest way to run Firecrawl yourself. If you really want the full Firecrawl server with its own queues, workers and databases, all of it still lives in this repo and you can run it on your own infrastructure. If you'd rather not run anything yourself, <a href=\"https://github.com/firecrawl/firecrawl#firecrawl-cloud\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Firecrawl Cloud</a> gives you every feature with no setup.</p>\n<p>The server runs with Docker Compose alongside Redis, PostgreSQL and a browser service, and the <a href=\"https://docs.firecrawl.dev/contributing/self-host\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">self-hosting guide</a> takes you from checkout to your first scrape.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/firecrawl/firecrawl/blob/main/SELF_HOST.md\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">SELF_HOST.md</a> lists the services and settings for the revision you checked out, and larger deployments can start from the <a href=\"https://github.com/firecrawl/firecrawl/blob/main/examples/kubernetes/cluster-install\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Kubernetes manifests</a> or the <a href=\"https://github.com/firecrawl/firecrawl/blob/main/examples/kubernetes/firecrawl-helm\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Helm chart</a>. Alexandria runs on Firecrawl Cloud, so the self-hosted server does not include it.</p>\n<hr />",
    "truncated": false,
    "chars": 1042
   },
